<div class="page-content">
    <h1>The Art of <i>Hollywood, Ending</i></h1>

    <p>
    These are the pieces of visual art that are referenced in <i>Hollywood, Ending</i>. List compiled by resident artist and nerdfighter Lauren (@potterygeek). View her original slideshow <a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1ItrgghSNQG2KH2v8Lfkf3bamL0ZSVGQLtaz8hynzcAk/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.
    </p>

    <p>[Captions in progress!!! Existing are placeholders.]</p>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/01-sans-neige-joan-mitchell.jpg" alt="Sans Neige, Joan Mitchell" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Joan Mitchell, <i>Sans Neige</i></h3>
        <p>This is the first piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/4a3a49c7-8181-437f-a079-5620f5c20147" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Joan Mitchell, Sans Neige (Triptych) 1969</a>. Page 62)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/02-farallon-island-albert-bierstadt.jpg" alt="Albert Bierstadt, Farallon Island" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Albert Bierstadt, <i>Farallon Island</i></h3>
        <p>This is the second piece of artwork. Not mentioned by name, but is an example of a “19th century nature-y” painting.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/11e4cb25-0960-4ca8-b9f6-bd1fbf192a59" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Albert Bierstadt, Farallon Island, 1887</a>. Page 64)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/03-untitled-kerry-james-marshall.jpg" alt="Kerry James Marshall, Untitled" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Kerry James Marshall, <i>Untitled</i></h3>
        <p>This is the third piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/d93f17fb-fca8-403f-8a2b-e85e5d43f35f" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kerry James Marshall, Untitled (Gallery), 2016</a>. Page 64)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/04-last-supper-andy-warhol.jpg" alt="Andy Warhol, Last Supper" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Andy Warhol, <i>Last Supper</i></h3>
        <p>This is the fourth piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_Supper_(Warhol)" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Andy Warhol, Last Supper, 1986</a>. Page 73)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

