    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/06-stadia-ii-julie-mehretu.jpg" alt="Julie Mehretu, Stadia II" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Julie Mehretu, <i>Stadia II</i></h3>
        <p>This is the sixth piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/3229aff9-ee40-4ef0-9789-106221a25892 " target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Julie Mehretu, Stadia II, 2004</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/07-water-lilies-claude-monet.jpg" alt="Claude Monet, Water Lilies (Nymphéas)" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Claude Monet, <i>Water Lilies (Nymphéas)</i></h3>
        <p>This is the seventh piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/7053d468-bf1f-42c9-b5bd-c7ccdb335c66 " target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Monet, Water Lilies (Nymphéas), 1915-1926</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/08-wheat-fields-after-the-rain-vincent-van-gogh.jpg" alt="Vincent van Gogh, Wheat Fields after the Rain (The Plain of Auvers)" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Vincent van Gogh, <i>Wheat Fields after the Rain (The Plain of Auvers)</i> and <i>Le Moulin de la Galette</i></h3>
        <p>This is the eighth piece of artwork. Work not mentioned by title, could be either.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/3c5512b1-e195-4b77-9671-f8c1e73e9b25" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vincent van Gogh, Wheat Fields after the Rain (The Plain of Auvers), 1890</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/09-le-moulin-de-la-galette-vincent-van-gogh.jpg" alt="Vincent van Gogh, Le Moulin de la Galette" imageSide="left">
        
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/01fd8421-c117-4309-8f99-b08b7bacec79" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vincent van Gogh, Le Moulin de la Galette, 1886-87</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/10-the-port-of-trouville-eugene-louis-boudin.jpg" alt="Eugène Louis Boudin, The Port of Trouville (Le Port de Trouville)" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Eugène Louis Boudin, <i>The Port of Trouville (Le Port de Trouville)</i></h3>
        <p>This is the ninth piece of artwork. No title mentioned so there’s a few more it could be, to see more here is a <a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/?searchbox=%22Boudin%22" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">link</a>.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/f580b37b-0422-4797-8bc1-86247b2255a6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Eugène Louis Boudin, The Port of Trouville (Le Port de Trouville), 1882</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/11-untitled-no-9-agnes-martin.jpg" alt="Agnes Martin, Untitled No. 9" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Agnes Martin, <i>Untitled No. 9</i></h3>
        <p>This is the tenth piece of artwork. No title work mentioned, but here is one for fun (zoom in).</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://collection.carnegieart.org/objects/2a691fe3-4b70-467a-8d9a-1d974e058f78" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agnes Martin, Untitled No. 9, 1977</a>. Page 85)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/12-untitled-jean-michel-basquiat-andy-warhol.jpg" alt="Andy Warhol and Jean Michel Basquiat Collaboration, Untitled" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Andy Warhol and Jean Michel Basquiat Collaboration, <i>Untitled</i></h3>
        <p>This is the eleventh piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://warhol.netx.net/portals/warhol-exhibitions/#asset/131424" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Andy Warhol and Jean Michel Basquiat Collaboration, Untitled, 1984-85</a>. Page 203)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/13-with-my-back-to-the-world-agnes-martin.jpg" alt="Agnes Martin, With My Back to the World" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Agnes Martin, <i>With My Back to the World</i></h3>
        <p>This is the twelfth piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79892" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agnes Martin, With My Back to the World, 1997</a>. Page 203)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/14-single-dollar-sign-andy-warhol.jpg" alt="Andy Warhol, Single Dollar Sign - $ (1) FS II.275" imageSide="right">
        <h3>Andy Warhol, <i>Single Dollar Sign - $ (1) FS II.275</i></h3>
        <p>This is the thirteenth piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://www.artsy.net/artwork/andy-warhol-single-dollar-sign-dollars-1-fs-ii-dot-275-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Andy Warhol, Single Dollar Sign - $ (1) FS II.275, 1958</a>. Page 215)</span>
    </TextAndImage>

    <TextAndImage src="/images/artwork-ref/15-big-electric-chair-andy-warhol.jpg" alt="Andy Warhol, Big Electric Chair" imageSide="left">
        <h3>Andy Warhol, <i>Big Electric Chair</i></h3>
        <p>This is the fourteenth piece of artwork.</p>
        <span slot="caption">(<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Electric_Chair" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Andy Warhol, Big Electric Chair, 1967</a>. Page ?)</span>
